    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.75,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.73 from 7 h to 18 h. If the reader were saturating, diluted aliquots would read well above the undiluted value once scaled back up. I tested the 18 h aliquot at three dilutions. The 3x dilution read 0.2435, or 0.73 scaled. The 10x dilution read 0.0766, or 0.77 scaled (replicates 0.0763 and 0.077). The 30x dilution read 0.0253, or 0.76 scaled (replicates 0.0229 and 0.0277, noisier). All three fall within about 5% of the undiluted 0.73. The slight excess is small and consistent with noise or minor non-linearity, so the plateau reflects real stationary phase and the biomass is at the level the undiluted readings indicate."
  },
